														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1483508">
									

<p>There's an internal logic at play here, though. He knows to capitalize names and the first word of a sentence, but he doesn't capitalize I unless it's the first word. He knows that you have to end a sentence with a period, but there's very little punctuation besides. There are no apostrophes, for instance, though I think I saw a comma.</p>
<p>Anyway, it's obvious that he's learning writing in a very piecemeal fashion. But the consistency of the writing to its own logic is one of the most charming things about this, I thought.</p>

							</div>

								
					
